#### Track selection and PID

\(D\)-mesons were studied using the HFT to directly reconstruct the decay from the daughter particles in the channels [66]:

* \(D^{0}(\overline{D^{0}})\to K^{\mp}\pi^{\pm}\), B.R. \((3.93\pm 0.04)\%\), \(c\tau=122.9\)\(\mu\)m
* \(D^{\pm}\to K^{\mp}2\pi^{\pm}\), B.R. \((9.46\pm 0.24)\%\), \(c\tau=311.8\)\(\mu\)m

Global tracks are used to reconstruct charm meson candidates given that these daughter tracks should appear to come from a displaced vertex relative to the primary. The following criteria were used to select and assure the quality of daughter candidates in the analysis:

* Transverse momentum \(p_{\rm T}>0.2\) GeV/c.
* Within HFT acceptance \(|\eta|<1\).

